{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#866","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#866","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#866\",\"parent_revision\":\"c137ac4cb287bd425c6cf775edd7c3fad566e2337a4ee4b60b27235766fa757c\",\"root_revision\":\"c137ac4cb287bd425c6cf775edd7c3fad566e2337a4ee4b60b27235766fa757c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement the WebSocket server (`WS /ws`) using starlette.websockets with a connection manager supporting rooms (per-VM, per-job). Implement the event types: `job_created`, `job_updated`, `step_added`, `screenshot_captured`, `vm_state_changed`, `fleet_status`, `inspector_report`, `steering_message`, `todo_updated`. Connect to the event ingest webhook so MCP tool pushes broadcast to connected clients.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **dashboard websocket server with event bus** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PRD-vm-flightsimulator-v2\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c85bfb3e424eb2357af0b6de4d744a64ea0b18155e1f8dbb7ffefae2dcab8477\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVDCy1A\"}"}